WEBVTT

00:02.140 --> 00:03.390
Listen, Usami.

00:03.650 --> 00:05.600
We're here as scouts, nothing more.

00:06.410 --> 00:10.070
Don't try anything before 
Lt. Tsurumi gets here.

00:10.070 --> 00:13.310
If we waste time, he might escape.

00:13.620 --> 00:17.500
There's a chance that Hijikata and his 
friends have heard about the serial killings

00:17.500 --> 00:19.790
and come to Sapporo themselves.

00:20.140 --> 00:22.540
We can't handle all of them on our own.

00:25.430 --> 00:26.770
Look, Kirawus.

00:26.770 --> 00:28.130
Somebody dropped some money.

00:31.010 --> 00:31.670
What's wrong?

00:32.680 --> 00:36.930
I just thought I heard the 
voice of a dead man I knew.

00:39.340 --> 00:40.770
One sen!

00:40.770 --> 00:43.270
This is the first spot good luck you've 
ever had in your life.

00:44.380 --> 00:49.020
Sapporo is swarming with 
police after the murders,

00:49.530 --> 00:53.530
and there are tons of people from 
Tsukisappu in the red-light district.

00:54.000 --> 00:57.050
Lieutenant Tsurumi's men could easily be here.

00:57.730 --> 01:00.950
It's not easy to flee 
the grim reaper forever.

01:02.020 --> 01:03.540
Private Ogata.

01:03.540 --> 01:06.430
So you betrayed Lieutenant Tsurumi.

01:07.020 --> 01:08.400
I never saw that coming.

01:08.860 --> 01:12.380
I never thought you'd betray him, either.

01:13.500 --> 01:17.590
Why don't you disguise 
yourselves as peddlers again?

01:22.570 --> 01:26.810
Has a strange Japanese man come to 
this village talking about gold?

01:27.250 --> 01:29.200
One with strange tattoos.

01:29.200 --> 01:34.400
Not here, but I did hear someone talking 
about a strange man with tattoos

01:34.400 --> 01:36.070
they saw at the Utashinai coal mines.

01:36.070 --> 01:39.490
He was a peddler, 
selling sweets or something.

01:41.440 --> 01:44.410
Candy! Sweet candy!

01:44.410 --> 01:47.410
You, young man! Want a taste?

01:47.730 --> 01:48.540
Really?

01:48.540 --> 01:51.140
Of course! Put out your hand.

01:51.930 --> 01:52.800
Here.

01:53.970 --> 01:55.690
Coal?

01:57.840 --> 02:00.720
The look on your face! I love it!

02:02.090 --> 02:04.810
Sorry, sorry. Forgive me.

02:04.810 --> 02:08.200
Actually, I've got something much 
better than candy to give you.

02:08.200 --> 02:09.780
Come with me.

02:09.780 --> 02:12.150
Really? What could be better than candy?

02:12.150 --> 02:15.540
You'll have to see for yourself!

02:54.960 --> 03:03.660
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

03:46.470 --> 03:51.270
<b>Episode Forty-Seven
Steamship</b>

03:52.500 --> 03:59.800
Buy some sweets! Just two rin a bag!

04:00.090 --> 04:01.460
Hey, candy seller with the octopus.

04:01.460 --> 04:04.260
I'll buy some sweets, so will 
you take your clothes off?

04:05.130 --> 04:06.140
Why?

04:06.650 --> 04:11.640
'Cause I want to see what 
your nipples look like.

04:11.940 --> 04:16.260
I give you candy, and you give 
me the money to pay for it.

04:16.260 --> 04:19.050
Which means I'd be showing you 
my nipples for free, right?

04:19.050 --> 04:20.480
I don't need the candy, then.

04:20.480 --> 04:23.230
My nipples aren't cheap, you know!

04:23.230 --> 04:23.970
Yup, yup!

04:25.220 --> 04:26.120
That's freezing cold!

04:26.120 --> 04:27.600
Sorry, sorry.

04:27.600 --> 04:28.700
You should change.

04:28.700 --> 04:30.620
Don't touch me, shithead!

04:30.830 --> 04:32.290
There's something weird about these guys!

04:32.510 --> 04:34.810
Our rivals must've sent them 
to mess up our business!

04:34.810 --> 04:36.880
Beat the piss out of them!

04:39.840 --> 04:41.340
No!

04:41.550 --> 04:43.160
Stop!

04:50.810 --> 04:55.270
Hey, kid, you seen any 
guys with weird tattoos?

04:55.490 --> 04:57.790
Yeah, over there.

04:57.790 --> 04:59.320
What? Really?

05:04.730 --> 05:06.280
Gimme candy.

05:12.770 --> 05:16.650
Watch carefully! I'll make the candy appear!

05:16.650 --> 05:18.710
Aw, no way!

05:23.130 --> 05:28.720
Hey, peddler, I heard you 
had some strange tattoos.

05:33.960 --> 05:35.520
I'd love to see them.

05:38.440 --> 05:39.930
Okay!

05:38.870 --> 05:41.190
<b>Great Evil</b>

05:42.510 --> 05:44.990
Your whole face is covered in tattoos?

05:45.410 --> 05:49.020
Great stuff, right? I did them all myself!

05:49.020 --> 05:51.700
All by yourself?

05:51.700 --> 05:56.410
What? So this is what they 
meant by weird tattoos?

06:03.850 --> 06:05.290
I love the look on your face!

06:09.420 --> 06:11.330
Sorry to bug you.

06:11.850 --> 06:15.520
<b>Shiriuchi River
Toppu River
Sorachi River
Saru River</b>

06:11.850 --> 06:15.520
<b>Toppu River</b>

06:11.850 --> 06:15.520
<b>Sapporo</b>

06:11.850 --> 06:15.520
<b>Shiriuchi
 River</b>

06:11.850 --> 06:15.520
<b>Present Location</b>

06:12.460 --> 06:15.520
I guess now we head south to the Saru River?

06:13.660 --> 06:15.520
<b>Saru River</b>

06:16.380 --> 06:19.220
I'm curious about those 
murders in Sapporo, too.

06:19.220 --> 06:22.060
We could head there first, too.

06:22.060 --> 06:27.400
I loved the disappointed look 
on the face of Boss Wakayama!

06:30.810 --> 06:34.590
You'll never find the gold!

06:35.430 --> 06:38.540
Sweets! Buy some sweets!

06:41.450 --> 06:46.590
Asirpa-chan, you're sure he said that
we'll never find the gold?

06:46.930 --> 06:50.380
That's how it sounded to me... I think.

06:52.580 --> 06:53.770
What do we do?

06:53.770 --> 06:58.780
Give up on the pirate and 
look for the peddler instead?

06:58.780 --> 07:01.850
We should've stripped him 
naked just to be safe.

07:02.960 --> 07:05.710
I guess we'll head to Sapporo.

07:05.710 --> 07:09.040
We'll take a ship down the 
Ishikari River to Ebetsu.

07:09.040 --> 07:09.950
A ship?

07:10.190 --> 07:12.770
The roads are all muddy 
from the melting snow.

07:12.770 --> 07:16.330
Ships are faster and easier.

07:16.330 --> 07:18.700
<b>Toppu River Area Ainu Village</b>

07:17.230 --> 07:23.040
I heard a rumor that you might know where 
the Ainu hid their gold many years ago.

07:23.490 --> 07:25.690
Your brother was involved, wasn't he?

07:26.790 --> 07:30.720
I've heard that some villain 
killed him and his comrades,

07:30.720 --> 07:32.510
then moved the gold.

07:33.080 --> 07:36.100
Where? You know, right?

07:37.350 --> 07:38.470
I do.

07:38.900 --> 07:43.900
Pirate, how much do we believe this guy?

07:44.750 --> 07:50.110
You must've heard where the gold 
they buried was found, right?

07:52.240 --> 07:55.490
Several rivers, I heard.

07:56.130 --> 08:02.330
Toppu. Sorachi. Saru. Shiriuchi.

08:03.110 --> 08:06.840
That matches the names he gave perfectly.

08:06.840 --> 08:10.630
So, where did they put it?

08:13.690 --> 08:14.580
Gondo.

08:14.580 --> 08:15.300
Yes?

08:15.570 --> 08:17.530
Bring me three more bushels' worth.

08:21.900 --> 08:24.060
We'll be at Ebetsu before noon.

08:24.480 --> 08:27.020
Mister Hood didn't want to ride with us?

08:27.280 --> 08:29.440
He wants to stay with the horses.

08:29.680 --> 08:33.350
He's probably keeping his distance 
from us so he can be ready

08:33.350 --> 08:36.900
if Ogata shows up to go after Asirpa-san.

08:37.360 --> 08:40.720
He probably thinks of her as bait.

08:46.080 --> 08:47.830
<b>Letters</b>

08:46.080 --> 08:47.830
<b>Official Business</b>

08:54.640 --> 08:56.100
Who are those guys?

08:56.820 --> 08:59.350
They're in front of us, and not by accident.

09:00.670 --> 09:03.600
We've been bribing everybody we 
could find in the Ainu villages.

09:04.740 --> 09:07.650
We need to do a job before we leave.

09:07.990 --> 09:12.070
You don't think it's those guys they're 
talking about that attack ships?

09:12.950 --> 09:15.110
It has to be.

09:15.110 --> 09:16.380
Well, screw 'em!

09:16.380 --> 09:18.010
We'll run them over!

09:26.910 --> 09:27.710
What?

09:29.030 --> 09:30.710
That's what you get!

09:58.000 --> 09:59.270
Stop the ship.

10:01.220 --> 10:02.080
Huh?

10:03.340 --> 10:04.450
The pirate!

10:06.930 --> 10:08.810
Is that you, Shiraishi?!

10:09.330 --> 10:11.540
Who are you guys?

10:11.850 --> 10:12.860
Be careful!

10:12.860 --> 10:14.380
Those two are with him!

10:14.380 --> 10:16.880
No! We're not!

10:18.970 --> 10:19.930
Stop!

10:21.240 --> 10:23.720
Stay put, you idiot! He'll shoot you!

10:25.120 --> 10:26.100
I don't have a choice!

10:32.610 --> 10:35.360
He's awfully nice.

10:35.770 --> 10:37.190
Hey, Shiraishi.

10:37.190 --> 10:40.210
You've got somebody pretty 
tough working for you.

10:40.210 --> 10:41.570
I like him.

10:45.770 --> 10:47.580
Another steamship's approaching.

10:48.320 --> 10:49.580
This is bad.

10:49.790 --> 10:54.090
<b>Kamiyamamaru</b>

10:54.360 --> 10:59.090
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

11:06.420 --> 11:08.170
<i>Hold it, Sugimoto!</i>

11:08.170 --> 11:09.290
<i>Don't kill him yet!</i>

11:09.290 --> 11:11.440
<i>I'll see if he has any info first!</i>

11:14.660 --> 11:17.610
<i>Oh, no! Sugimoto's about 
to go all murderous!</i>

11:17.610 --> 11:19.770
<i>He's all worked up for a kill!</i>

11:20.320 --> 11:26.830
We figured that somebody had to know 
where the Ainu first hid the gold,

11:26.830 --> 11:28.500
so we're looking for them.

11:28.500 --> 11:32.140
Oh, you too?

11:33.130 --> 11:35.930
So you heard the same thing, Shiraishi?

11:35.930 --> 11:38.920
The rumor that our tattoo 
code can't be solved anymore.

11:40.420 --> 11:44.270
Pirate, there's bad news coming 
in the ship ahead of us!

11:51.050 --> 11:52.190
Get the ship moving.

11:54.240 --> 11:55.880
He's got a gun!

11:55.880 --> 11:56.960
Robbers!

11:57.370 --> 12:00.650
Block the door and get 
on the floor, everyone.

12:01.170 --> 12:08.230
They'll regret choosing the 
ship I was aboard in hell.

12:07.780 --> 12:12.710
<b>Letters</b>

12:07.780 --> 12:12.710
<b>Official Business</b>

12:08.230 --> 12:12.710
<i>In those days, postal workers carried guns!</i>

12:24.170 --> 12:25.800
Don't try anything.

12:26.210 --> 12:28.640
Go! Go!

12:30.450 --> 12:32.350
Hey, open the door!

12:35.340 --> 12:38.060
For you, this river leads straight to hell!

12:42.320 --> 12:44.320
<b>Kamiyamamaru</b>

12:42.730 --> 12:44.320
A gunshot!

12:45.020 --> 12:46.680
Yes! He killed him!

12:46.680 --> 12:49.370
That postman kicks ass!

12:49.820 --> 12:55.310
<i>He'd been a postman for 35 years, 
and this was his first time firing a gun!</i>

12:56.290 --> 13:01.760
<i>But it was actually Vasily, who'd fired 
at the same time, who killed him.</i>

13:02.110 --> 13:03.220
Asirpa-san!

13:04.180 --> 13:06.340
Kiss my lead!

13:09.360 --> 13:11.240
The passengers are being attacked!

13:11.240 --> 13:12.390
Turn around! Turn around!

13:16.140 --> 13:18.060
Shit! They're coming after us!

13:18.820 --> 13:20.020
Let me take over.

13:26.950 --> 13:28.490
What the hell?

13:28.490 --> 13:30.010
They're ramming us!

13:54.600 --> 13:58.010
Haha! Did you see that, Shiraishi?

13:58.010 --> 14:00.940
Way to go, Pirate! You got away!

14:01.400 --> 14:04.650
You can send your next 
letter from hell, maggots!

14:07.770 --> 14:09.610
I found this gun!

14:10.820 --> 14:13.900
I'm the postman from hell!

14:16.890 --> 14:18.370
He's the craziest guy on this ship!

14:18.370 --> 14:21.460
Pirate, we lost three men!

14:23.060 --> 14:24.550
Who killed them?

14:24.550 --> 14:28.840
There's a crazy postman 
on the passenger deck!

14:35.550 --> 14:37.120
I've only got one bullet left.

14:37.500 --> 14:38.520
Are there any other bullets?

14:39.060 --> 14:42.520
The pack that the soldier who had 
the gun was carrying is over there!

14:42.520 --> 14:44.610
Don't! It's not in there!

14:47.990 --> 14:50.780
You're gonna pay for killing my citizens.

14:54.520 --> 14:56.040
Asirpa-san, get down!

14:58.800 --> 14:59.700
Get down!

15:10.880 --> 15:12.090
Hey.

15:17.270 --> 15:20.100
That put Asirpa-san in danger, shithead!

15:29.690 --> 15:34.160
I'm delivering your conscription 
notice... to hell!

15:34.160 --> 15:36.200
Die!

15:37.840 --> 15:40.000
I'm gonna kill this asshole no matter what.

15:41.390 --> 15:42.420
I'm out of bullets?

15:42.680 --> 15:44.220
There's more ammo over here!

15:44.220 --> 15:45.210
Hurry! Hurry!

15:49.410 --> 15:50.760
Where is it?

15:55.450 --> 15:56.140
Get away!

15:58.320 --> 15:59.530
That asshole!

16:06.320 --> 16:07.190
Sugimoto!

16:07.520 --> 16:09.480
Asirpa-san, are you okay?

16:10.760 --> 16:16.160
Pirate, the postman who was firing 
at us left the money and ran.

16:16.160 --> 16:19.410
Sugimoto, there's something 
you want to ask him, right?

16:23.310 --> 16:26.330
Your name's Sugimoto, huh?

16:31.400 --> 16:36.190
A little over a year ago, I met one of 
the other escaped prisoners,

16:36.190 --> 16:38.930
a yakuza boss named Wakayama, in Sapporo.

16:39.840 --> 16:43.320
I got close to him intending 
to kill him and strip his skin.

16:43.320 --> 16:45.900
But I got surrounded by his men.

16:46.490 --> 16:49.270
You won't be able to crack the tattoo code.

16:50.190 --> 16:51.780
Why?

16:52.050 --> 16:54.180
I mean, it's possible you 
might end up feeding the fishes

16:54.180 --> 16:57.200
after you drown in the ocean somewhere.

16:57.550 --> 17:00.740
Or eaten by a bear.

17:02.590 --> 17:08.770
Or perhaps... some weirdo 
might ruin everything.

17:11.660 --> 17:19.530
The fact that he didn't strip off my skin 
means he's certain that it was worthless.

17:22.280 --> 17:27.210
That ties in with what Asirpa-chan 
heard that peddler say!

17:29.380 --> 17:33.030
That's why I gave up on finding the skins.

17:33.030 --> 17:36.780
So did you find the place 
where the Ainu hid it?

17:38.420 --> 17:40.660
What do you think?

17:43.050 --> 17:46.420
It's true that finding it would 
get you closer to the gold.

17:46.420 --> 17:50.970
But I can't imagine Nopperabo hiding 
the gold someplace easily found.

17:51.520 --> 17:55.920
Sometimes you can't even find the change 
you put into your own pocket, right?

17:56.770 --> 17:59.560
So why don't we work together?

17:59.560 --> 18:02.930
I liked you, Shiraishi. 
You were always a lot of fun.

18:04.010 --> 18:07.550
And I like strong men like you, Sugimoto.

18:08.730 --> 18:11.230
We're gonna end up fighting over the gold.

18:12.030 --> 18:15.070
How about you become upper-class 
citizens in my country, then?

18:15.930 --> 18:19.450
You're just another weirdo
 talking about nonsense.

18:22.380 --> 18:27.360
I'm gonna be a king on a warm island 
in the South Pacific somewhere!

18:27.920 --> 18:30.680
I'll grow fruits to sell to other countries,

18:30.680 --> 18:33.670
maybe even put my face on the currency!

18:34.010 --> 18:37.890
I'll have a lot of kids and build a kingdom
 where my family can live!

18:37.890 --> 18:39.050
Great idea, huh?

18:39.260 --> 18:42.160
You did used to talk about that all the time.

18:44.480 --> 18:48.390
Why does everyone want to bear the burden 
of something as big as a country?

18:48.630 --> 18:50.890
Sugimoto, do you have a family?

18:51.960 --> 18:53.120
No, not really.

18:53.430 --> 18:56.400
Did you kill them all, maybe?

18:59.900 --> 19:01.820
Did you?

19:01.820 --> 19:03.300
I did not!

19:04.760 --> 19:05.910
Tuberculosis got them.

19:07.670 --> 19:09.290
Enough about this.

19:12.590 --> 19:14.160
Then you understand.

19:14.610 --> 19:17.340
I lost my whole family to smallpox.

19:17.970 --> 19:19.960
Nobody talks to you.

19:19.960 --> 19:21.530
Nobody brings it up.

19:22.240 --> 19:24.600
I ended up an outsider in my hometown.

19:25.100 --> 19:28.070
So I thought like a child would...

19:28.070 --> 19:31.770
If I make my own country, 
then nobody can kick me out of it!

19:32.060 --> 19:33.940
A king, huh?

19:35.390 --> 19:37.720
Have dreams! Look forward to the future!

19:37.720 --> 19:40.080
I gave up on living in fear.

19:40.450 --> 19:43.780
And maybe that's why I was the 
only one who didn't get infected.

19:43.780 --> 19:45.700
I was so cheerful,
 the disease couldn't touch me!

19:51.670 --> 19:57.460
Saichi, don't count on there being 
any open beds at the clinic.

19:57.890 --> 20:00.300
I won't last long enough to see one, anyway.

20:01.010 --> 20:02.850
You're a kind man.

20:03.770 --> 20:08.140
And so you always get 
stuck with the worst jobs.

20:08.740 --> 20:12.530
And I've always been a nosy man.

20:13.230 --> 20:17.820
When your personality's like that,
 it doesn't change easily.

20:18.310 --> 20:21.870
I'll go back to the hospital 
in the morning and ask again.

20:32.410 --> 20:36.410
I thought black cats were supposed 
to prevent tuberculosis.

20:38.370 --> 20:40.300
So you're as useless as I am, huh?

20:49.490 --> 20:51.010
Leave home.

20:51.680 --> 20:54.340
Don't let the disease get you like it did us.

20:55.130 --> 20:57.530
Leave me.

20:58.330 --> 21:04.700
It's not a bad thing to 
live your own life, Saichi.

21:05.860 --> 21:10.700
<i>Go and find a place where you can be happy.</i>

21:16.430 --> 21:17.880
I won't let this beat me.

21:24.270 --> 21:25.970
Come on and try to kill me!

21:26.460 --> 21:28.330
I'm immortal!

21:30.570 --> 21:36.600
What were you going to do to make yourself 
happy after you found the gold?

21:37.510 --> 21:39.240
Don't you have any dreams?

21:40.660 --> 21:43.610
Pirate! We're almost to Ebetsu!

21:43.830 --> 21:46.530
I do apologize for the trouble, everyone.

21:46.530 --> 21:52.660
As our way of saying sorry, 
we won't take your valuables.

21:52.660 --> 21:57.170
<b>Letters</b>

21:52.660 --> 21:57.170
<b>Official Business</b>

21:53.160 --> 21:57.170
We'll just take the money 
from the registered mail.

23:35.450 --> 23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Discharge</b>

23:36.250 --> 23:38.930
Next time: "Discharge"!
